        "original_id": "9c641d99-17be-5f21-85ec-566c5b20676f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1982 Cannes Film Festival\n- Films: Missing, Yol\n- People: Costa-Gavras, Şerif Gören, Yılmaz Güney, Sissy Spacek, Jack Lemmon, Melanie Mayron, John Shea, Janice Rule, Charles Cioffi, Charles Horman, Salvador Allende\n- Topics: 1973 Chilean coup\n\nFacts:\n- In 1973, the US-backed Chilean coup deposed democratically elected socialist President Salvador Allende.\n- In the aftermath of the 1973 Chilean coup, American journalist Charles Horman disappeared.\n- Missing is a 1982 American historical drama film directed by Costa-Gavras.\n- Missing stars Sissy Spacek, Jack Lemmon, Melanie Mayron, John Shea, Janice Rule, and Charles Cioffi.\n- Missing is based on the true story of Charles Horman.\n- The 35th Cannes Film Festival was held from 14 to 26 May 1982.\n- At the 1982 Cannes Film Festival, the Palme d'Or was jointly awarded to Missing by Costa Gavras and Yol by Şerif Gören and Yılmaz Güney.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
